# Generated files are compared byte-for-byte against what the tools produce, and the tools write
# LF. Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF on checkout
# and every --check reports stale on a clean tree.
#
# Normalising the whole repository rather than just the generated files keeps the rule simple and
# avoids the next generated file being forgotten.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, in case a PDF or an image is ever added alongside a publication node.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
